<title>USA: Brazil trade gap will not hit $15 bln in 97--Malan.</title>
<headline>Brazil trade gap will not hit $15 bln in 97--Malan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's international trade deficit will be larger in 1997 than in 1996, but it will not reach $15.0 billion in the current year, Finance Minister Pedro Malan said.</p>
<p>&quot;The trade deficit is not going to be $15.0 billion&quot; in 1997, Malan told reporters at The Council on Foreign Relations here. He reiterated, however, the 1997 trade gap &quot;will be worse than in 1996.&quot;</p>
</text>
